M5_equilibrium_law: can the galaxy law be the equilibrium (attractor) of a normally self-gravitating medium?

Frozen criteria: FROZEN_CRITERIA.md (a364a6df13). kappa = 1/2 FITTED. Footings never pooled. Cold energy = medium of
real rest mass, no particle. Not "theory closed". Nothing here says the data favour the framework.
Run: OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 nice -n 15 python3 m5_equilibrium_law.py [--mutate]
mutate=False

=== S1  3D existence: the law's stress (AQUAL minus Newton) balances the phantom on any Phi
S1 PASS  value=5.72e-39  line=<=1e-12  [relative residual of div(Pi) - rho_ph grad Phi at 20 random points, quartic Phi, random a0]

=== S2  uniqueness (spherical jets, then 3D jets): the stress cannot respond to rho_c
  spherical: coefficient of g'' = A_rho * (-g*Derivative(M(g), g) - M(g) + 1)/(4*pi*G)  ->  A_rho = [0]
  dP_par/dg forced = [g*(-g*Derivative(M(g), g) - M(g) + 1)/(4*pi*G)]  ;  P_perp = A - g h/4piG, d/drho = 0: True
  3D: third-derivative coefficients force (A_rho, B_rho) = [{A_r: 0, B_r: 0}]; then [{A_s: -chi/(8*pi*G), B3: chi/(4*pi*G), B_s: chi_s/(4*pi*G)}]
S2 PASS  value=sph True,True,True; 3D True,True  line=all True  [exact-law equilibrium for every baryon profile forces a stress that does not depend on rho_c; unique up to a constant pressure]

=== S3  the spherical balance integrates to mu(g/a0) g = G M_b/r^2 (unique by regularity)
S3 PASS  value=0  line=0  [balance == -(g/4piG r^2) [ (r^2 mu g)' - 4piG r^2 rho_b ]  =>  mu g = G M_b/r^2 + C/r^2, C=0]

=== S4  dynamics of a medium held up by a density-blind stress (Cowling, 1D along the field)
  background (c2=0, T_b' = rho0 g): 0
  rho-blind: xi_tt = g*Derivative(xi(x), x) + g*xi(x)*Derivative(rho0(x), x)/rho0(x)
  + c2:      xi_tt = (c2*xi(x)*Derivative(rho0(x), (x, 2)) + 2*c2*Derivative(rho0(x), x)*Derivative(xi(x), x) + g*xi(x)*Derivative(rho0(x), x) + (c2*Derivative(xi(x), (x, 2)) + g*Derivative(xi(x), x))*rho0(x))/rho0(x)
S4 PASS  value=coef xi'=g, coef xi''(c2 case)=c2  line=g and c2  [principal symbol s^2 = i k g (|Re s| ~ sqrt(kg/2), Hadamard ill-posed); with c2: s^2 = -c2 k^2 + i k g]

=== S5/S6  force on the medium; deep-regime cancellation; linear FRW growth
S5 PASS  value=(drho_b - mterm - rhobar)/(drho_c + rhobar)  line=-(rhobar - drho_b + mterm)/(rhobar + drho_c)  [per-mass force on the medium = -[(rhobar - drho_b + div(mu grad dPhi)/4piG)/(rhobar + drho_c)] grad dPhi; mu-term O(g/a0)]
S6 PASS  value=-1  line=-1  [linear order: force per mass = -grad dPhi, so delta'' + 2H delta' = 4piG rhobar delta (dust)]

